{
    "info": {
        "name": "Stickers & Labels - box sticker + location labels",
        "_postman_id": "7f3a1c62-5b0e-4d18-9a44-2c6b8e0d1f33",
        "description": "The box sticker's face on FIXED data - no carton, no tenant, no auth.\n\nGET /api/p2p/spi/sticker-preview\n\nIt 404s outside local/debug, because it prints a signed QR for a box that does not exist.\n\nQuery flags switch the variants the design has to survive:\n  cold=1        cold-chain symbol (temp= sets the band)\n  haz=3         hazard symbol, class 3\n  fragile=1     fragile symbol\n  nostack=1     do-not-stack symbol\n  empty=1       every reference absent - the all-dashes case\n  condition=    the chip in the header\n  html=1        HTML instead of a PDF, to iterate faster\n  format=json   the payload the blade is handed\n  raw=1         with format=json, the full data: URIs\n\npictos[] holds 0 to 4 entries - only the symbols that apply.\n\n--- LOCATION LABELS ---\nWarehouse / Zone / Rack / Shelf, 4in x 3in each.\n\nLayout: what it is on the header left, handling flags on the header right\n(COLD CHAIN, HAZARDOUS, INACTIVE, or NORMAL when there are none - no logo),\nthe QR centred, then the code and the FULL ADDRESS IN IDS beneath it.\nA shelf prints WAREHOUSE / ZONE / RACK / SHELF, each under its own\nheading, because \"SH-003\" alone names a shelf in every warehouse the\nclient has.\n\nThese are tenant-scoped and need {{token}}. /label returns the printable\nPDF; /qr returns the bare PNG for a screen that places it itself.\n\nEach location has THREE endpoints:\n  /preview  JSON for the on-screen modal (includes qr + download_url)\n  /label    the printable A4 PDF\n  /qr       the bare PNG, for a screen that places it itself",
        "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
    },
    "variable": [
        {
            "key": "baseUrl",
            "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000",
            "type": "string"
